      "recipe_time": "Total: ~10 min",
      "recipe_notes": "Each piece is approximately 160\u2013190 kcal. Rice paper is gluten-free and much lighter than classic pide dough. For extra crispiness, pan-fry briefly before finishing in the oven or air fryer. Cheese topping is optional.",
      "source_language": "German",
      "translation": "Rice Paper Pide in 10 Minutes for Your Diet \ud83c\uddf9\ud83c\uddf7\u2728\nApproximately 160\u2013190 kcal per piece\n\nTurkish food can also help with weight loss \u2013 this recipe combines tradition with smart lightness:\n\nRice paper is gluten-free and much lighter than classic dough.\nGround meat provides high-quality protein for lasting satiety and muscle building.\nOnion, garlic, and parsley add flavor and valuable plant compounds.\nEggs ensure a perfect consistency and additional protein.\n\nExactly these kinds of recipes helped me\nlose 30 kilos and regulate my body \u2013 not through dieting, but through smart nutrition.\n\n\ud83d\udc49 For clean eating & real health knowledge\nfollow @ekins.healthy.life \ud83c\udf3f\n\n\ud83e\udd6c INGREDIENTS (5 pieces)\n\n\ud83e\udd63 DOUGH\n\u2022 10 sheets rice paper\n\u2022 2 eggs\n\u2022 Pinch of salt\n\n\ud83e\udd69 FILLING\n\u2022 500 g ground meat\n\u2022 1 small onion\n\u2022 1 clove garlic\n\u2022 3\u20134 tbsp tomato paste\n\u2022 1 tsp red pepper paste\n\u2022 \u00bd red bell pepper\n\u2022 Parsley\n\u2022 Salt, pepper, sweet paprika\n\n\u2728 TOPPING\n\u2022 Sesame seeds\n\u2022 Black cumin (nigella seeds)\n\u2022 Small cherry tomatoes or bell pepper\n\u2022 Optional: a little grated cheese\n\n\ud83d\udc69\u200d\ud83c\udf73 PREPARATION\n\nWhisk the eggs and briefly dip the rice paper in.\nLayer two sheets on top of each other.\n\nSpread the ground meat mixture on top and fold the edges in slightly to create the typical pide shape.\n\nDecorate the edges with sesame seeds and black cumin and top with cherry tomatoes, bell pepper, or a little cheese as desired \u2728\n\nBake at 200 \u00b0C until everything is golden brown and crispy.\n\n\u2728 Tip:\nIf you like it extra crunchy, you can briefly pan-fry the rice paper pide first and then finish it in the oven or air fryer \ud83e\udd0d\n\n\ud83d\udcca Significantly lighter than classic pide \u2013 with more protein and fewer calories \ud83d\udcaa\n\n\u2728 Protein \u00b7 Gluten-free \u00b7 Low-calorie \u00b7 Satiating \u00b7 Healthy fats\n\nSave & recreate \ud83e\udd0d\n\n#healthyrecipes #weightloss #glutenfree #quickandeasy",
