            "reality": "The recipe uses 500g ground meat (beef/lamb, ~1,200\u20131,500 kcal total depending on fat content), 2 eggs (~140 kcal), 10 sheets rice paper (~350 kcal), tomato paste, pepper paste, cheese topping, and sesame. Divided by 5 pieces, a rough estimate yields approximately 340\u2013420 kcal per piece \u2014 roughly double the claimed range \u2014 especially if using standard 20% fat ground beef and any cheese. The 160\u2013190 kcal figure appears significantly understated unless very lean meat (e.g. <5% fat turkey mince) and no cheese are used, which is not specified. USDA data for 100g of 80/20 ground beef alone is ~254 kcal; 100g per piece of filling alone would exceed the total claimed calorie count.",
