            "reality": "Rice paper is indeed lower in calories than traditional yeast-based pide dough per gram (rice paper ~340 kcal/100g dry vs. yeast dough ~270\u2013300 kcal/100g baked). However, rice paper is used in very thin, small sheets (each ~8\u201310g), so the total calorie saving from the wrapper is modest \u2014 roughly 30\u201350 kcal per piece compared to a small pide portion. The claim is directionally true but the magnitude of the benefit is minor and should not be overstated as a major dietary advantage.",
