            "type": "dosage_safety",
            "detail": "The recipe instructs baking at 200\u00b0C until 'golden brown and crispy' without specifying an internal temperature for the ground meat filling. USDA recommends ground beef reach an internal temperature of 71\u00b0C (160\u00b0F) to be safe. Visual cues alone (golden/crispy exterior) are not reliable indicators of safe internal doneness for ground meat.",
