    "transcript": "Dave Ramsey. S-tier is what I would say, if I was an idiot, so F-tier. He is the rehab of finance. It works if you're in crisis, but telling people to avoid debt entirely is too rigid for building wealth today. Caleb Hammer. A-tier. I love the tough love approach. It makes people face reality and he tells people what they probably haven't been told to their face. Mark Tilbury. B-tier. Long game thinking, soothing English accent. Great for people who want to build real wealth over time. He's pretty consistent and trustworthy. Braden Shaw. S-tier. He's straightforward. He saved me a bunch of money on my taxes through tax mitigation and he has introduced me to a lot of wealthy people that I'm now learning from. S-tier. Your Rich BFF. A-tier. She's relatable, easy to understand, and a very good entry point for beginners. And she's super bubbly. She is the Wall Street girly. Call to Leap. Steve. D-tier. Not bad advice, but it feels like he's built more for brands than anything else. Vinny Rodriguez. C-tier. Digestible finance. Over 10 years in the mortgage industry, up and coming, and his grandmother still refers to him as handsome. Bottom line, not every finance influencer is built the same, so know who you're taking advice from.",
    "discord_message_id": 1523371493260525650,
    "created_at": 1783270466.6087809
  },
