      "key_takeaways": [
        "BICA is the local word for espresso in Lisbon; CIMBALINO is the same drink but the Porto term.",
        "GAL\u00c3O is a milky latte-style coffee in a tall glass (1:3 coffee-to-milk ratio), great for mornings.",
        "MEIA DE LEITE is half coffee, half milk \u2014 a popular, softer breakfast option.",
        "PINGADO adds just a drop of milk to espresso; ABATANADO is a longer, more diluted coffee.",
        "Always stand at the counter \u2014 it's cheaper (\u20ac0.80\u20131.20), faster, and the most local experience.",
        "Basic ordering phrases: 'Um caf\u00e9, por favor' (espresso), 'Sem a\u00e7\u00facar' (no sugar), 'Com leite' (with milk)."
