      "summary": "Ekin Sheho shares a 10-minute gluten-free, low-calorie twist on Turkish pide using rice paper instead of traditional dough, filled with a spiced ground beef mixture. Each piece is approximately 160\u2013190 kcal, making it a high-protein, diet-friendly alternative. The creator credits simple recipes like this with helping her lose 30 kg.",
      "key_takeaways": [
        "Use rice paper (double-layered, dipped in beaten egg) as a low-calorie, gluten-free substitute for traditional pide dough.",
        "Fill with a spiced ground beef mixture (tomato paste, pepper paste, onion, garlic, parsley) and fold into the classic pide boat shape.",
        "Bake at 200\u00b0C until golden and crispy; for extra crunch, briefly pan-fry first, then finish in the oven or air fryer.",
        "Each pide is roughly 160\u2013190 kcal with high protein and significantly fewer calories than classic pide.",
        "Top with sesame, nigella seeds, cherry tomatoes, peppers, and optional cheese for authentic flavor."
      ],
