    "content_summary": {
      "title": "Chicken Bacon Ranch Chopped Wrap | Provecho",
      "author": "domtuttobene",
      "platform": "provecho",
      "body_text": "Ingredients\n\n2 lbs chicken thighs\n\n1 head of lettuce\n\n1 tomato\n\n1 package of bacon\n\n\u00bc lb Pepper jack cheese\n\nRanch\n\nSalt\n\nPepper\n\ngarlic powder\n\npaprika\n\ntortilla\n\nDirections\n\n1\n\nSeason the chicken with salt, pepper, garlic powder, and paprika.\n\nchicken thighs\n\nSalt\n\nPepper\n\ngarlic powder\n\npaprika\n\n2\n\nGrill over medium-high heat for 5\u20137 minutes per side, or until it hits 165\u00b0F. Let it rest\n\n3\n\nWhile the chicken cooks, lay the bacon on a baking sheet and bake at 400\u00b0F for 12\u201315 minutes until crispy. Drain on a paper towel.\n\nof bacon\n\n4\n\nShred the lettuce and lay it down on a cutting board.\n\n1 head of lettuce\n\n5\n\nAdd the diced chicken, crispy bacon, pepper jack cheese, and sliced tomato on top of the lettuce.\n\n1 tomato\n\nPepper jack cheese\n\n6\n\nDrizzle a generous amount of ranch over everything and season with salt and pepper to taste.\n\nRanch\n\n7\n\nChop it all up together with a knife until it's fully mixed and bite-sized.\n\n8\n\nWarm your tortilla so it's soft and easy to fold, then scoop the mixture into the middle.\n\ntortilla\n\n9\n\nFold in the sides, roll it up tight, and toast it in a pan a couple minutes per side until golden and crispy.\n\n10\n\nCut it in half and enjoy!",
      "captions": null,
      "metadata": {
        "article_markdown": "\n```EmbedRelativeTo\nmedia://generic/84f5aa55ad31.jpg\n```\n\n\nIngredients\n\n2 lbs chicken thighs\n\n1 head of lettuce\n\n1 tomato\n\n1 package of bacon\n\n\u00bc lb Pepper jack cheese\n\nRanch\n\nSalt\n\nPepper\n\ngarlic powder\n\npaprika\n\ntortilla\n\nDirections\n\n1\n\nSeason the chicken with salt, pepper, garlic powder, and paprika.\n\nchicken thighs\n\nSalt\n\nPepper\n\ngarlic powder\n\npaprika\n\n2\n\nGrill over medium-high heat for 5\u20137 minutes per side, or until it hits 165\u00b0F. Let it rest\n\n3\n\nWhile the chicken cooks, lay the bacon on a baking sheet and bake at 400\u00b0F for 12\u201315 minutes until crispy. Drain on a paper towel.\n\nof bacon\n\n4\n\nShred the lettuce and lay it down on a cutting board.\n\n1 head of lettuce\n\n5\n\nAdd the diced chicken, crispy bacon, pepper jack cheese, and sliced tomato on top of the lettuce.\n\n1 tomato\n\nPepper jack cheese\n\n6\n\nDrizzle a generous amount of ranch over everything and season with salt and pepper to taste.\n\nRanch\n\n7\n\nChop it all up together with a knife until it's fully mixed and bite-sized.\n\n8\n\nWarm your tortilla so it's soft and easy to fold, then scoop the mixture into the middle.\n\ntortilla\n\n9\n\nFold in the sides, roll it up tight, and toast it in a pan a couple minutes per side until golden and crispy.\n\n10\n\nCut it in half and enjoy!",
        "recipe_data": null,
