      "body_text": "Ingredients\n\nChicken tenders\n\n1 head of lettuce\n\nBlue cheese crumbles\n\nBlue cheese dressing\n\nBuffalo sauce\n\ntortilla\n\nSpicy Garlic Buffalo Sauce:\n\n\u00bd cup buffalo sauce\n\n2 tbsp butter\n\nC\n\nCusos Spicy Garlic Buffalo\n\nDirections\n\n1\n\nCook the chicken tenders according to package instructions (bake or air fry) until they're golden and crispy all over.\n\nChicken tenders\n\n2\n\nWhile that cooks, melt the butter in a small pan over low heat. Add garlic powder and spicy garlic buffalo seasoning and stir for about a minute until fragrant.\n\n2 tbsp butter\n\n3\n\nPour in the buffalo sauce and stir until it's smooth and combined.\n\n\u00bd cup buffalo sauce\n\n4\n\nToss the hot crispy tenders in spicy garlic buffalo seasoning\n\n5\n\nShred the lettuce and lay it down on a cutting board.\n\n1 head of lettuce\n\n6\n\nAdd the tenders and blue cheese crumbles on top of the lettuce.\n\nBlue cheese crumbles\n\n7\n\nDrizzle with blue cheese dressing and a little extra buffalo sauce.\n\nBlue cheese dressing\n\nBuffalo sauce\n\n8\n\nChop it all up together with a knife until it's fully mixed and bite-sized.\n\n9\n\nWarm your tortilla so it's soft and easy to fold, then scoop the mixture into the middle.\n\ntortilla\n\n10\n\nFold in the sides, roll it up tight, and toast it in a pan a couple minutes per side until golden and crispy.\n\n11\n\nCut it in half and enjoy!",
      "captions": null,
