      "body_text": "Ingredients\n\nBbq Grilled Chicken Thighs:\n\nChicken thighs\n\nSalt\n\nPepper\n\nGarlic\n\nSmoked paprika\n\nOlive oil\n\n1 head lettuce\n\nBacon\n\nCheddar cheese\n\nBBQ sauce\n\nRanch\n\ntortilla\n\nDirections\n\n1\n\nSeason the chicken thighs with salt, pepper, garlic, smoked paprika, and olive oil, and grill over medium-high heat for 5- 7 minutes per side until they hit 165\u00b0F. Brush with BBQ sauce halfway through. Let them rest.\n\nChicken thighs\n\nSalt\n\nPepper\n\nGarlic\n\nSmoked paprika\n\nOlive oil\n\n2\n\nWhile the chicken cooks, lay the bacon on a baking sheet and bake at 400\u00b0F for 12\u201315 minutes until crispy. Drain on a paper towel.\n\nBacon\n\n3\n\nShred the lettuce and lay it down on a cutting board.\n\n1 head lettuce\n\n4\n\nAdd the chicken, crispy bacon, and shredded cheddar on top of the lettuce.\n\nCheddar cheese\n\n5\n\nDrizzle a generous amount of BBQ sauce and ranch over everything.\n\nBBQ sauce\n\nRanch\n\n6\n\nChop it all up together with a knife until it's fully mixed and bite-sized.\n\n7\n\nWarm your tortilla so it's soft and easy to fold, then scoop the mixture into the middle.\n\ntortilla\n\n8\n\nFold in the sides, roll it up tight, and toast it in a pan a couple minutes per side until golden and crispy.\n\n9\n\nCut it in half and enjoy!",
