      "body_text": "Ingredients\n\nNashville hot chicken tenders\n\n1 head lettuce\n\nAmerican cheese\n\nDill pickles\n\nRanch\n\ntortilla\n\nNashville Hot Oil:\n\n3 tbsp cayenne pepper\n\n1 tbsp paprika\n\n1 tbsp garlic powder\n\n1 tbsp salt\n\n2 tbsp brown sugar\n\n1 cup hot oil\n\nDirections\n\n1\n\nCook the chicken tenders according to package instructions (bake or air fry) until they're golden and crispy all over.\n\nNashville hot chicken tenders\n\n2\n\nWhile that cooks, warm the hot oil in a pan on low heat. Stir in the cayenne, paprika, garlic powder, salt, and brown sugar\n\n1 cup hot oil\n\n3 tbsp cayenne pepper\n\n1 tbsp paprika\n\n1 tbsp garlic powder\n\n1 tbsp salt\n\n2 tbsp brown sugar\n\n3\n\nToss the hot crispy tenders right in the sauce until fully coated.\n\n4\n\nShred the lettuce and lay it down on a cutting board.\n\n1 head lettuce\n\n5\n\nAdd the sauced tenders, American cheese, and pickles on top of the lettuce.\n\nAmerican cheese\n\nDill pickles\n\n6\n\nChop everything up together with a knife until it's all mixed and bite-sized.\n\n7\n\nDrizzle ranch over the top and mix again until creamy and combined.\n\nRanch\n\n8\n\nWarm your tortilla so it's soft, then scoop the mixture into the middle.\n\ntortilla\n\n9\n\nFold in the sides, roll it up tight, and toast it in a pan a couple minutes per side until golden.\n\n10\n\nCut it in half and enjoy!",
      "captions": null,
      "metadata": {
        "article_markdown": "\n```EmbedRelativeTo\nmedia://generic/91b942f6ce26.jpg\n```\n\n\nIngredients\n\nNashville hot chicken tenders\n\n1 head lettuce\n\n\n```EmbedRelativeTo\nmedia://generic/7777cadaea7e.webp\n```\n\n\nAmerican cheese\n\nDill pickles\n\nRanch\n\ntortilla\n\nNashville Hot Oil:\n\n3 tbsp cayenne pepper\n\n1 tbsp paprika\n\n1 tbsp garlic powder\n\n1 tbsp salt\n\n2 tbsp brown sugar\n\n1 cup hot oil\n\nDirections\n\n1\n\nCook the chicken tenders according to package instructions *(bake or air fry)* until they're golden and crispy all over.\n\nNashville hot chicken tenders\n\n2\n\nWhile that cooks, warm the hot oil in a pan on low heat. Stir in the cayenne, paprika, garlic powder, salt, and brown sugar\n\n1 cup hot oil\n\n3 tbsp cayenne pepper\n\n1 tbsp paprika\n\n1 tbsp garlic powder\n\n1 tbsp salt\n\n2 tbsp brown sugar\n\n3\n\nToss the hot crispy tenders right in the sauce until fully coated.\n\n4\n\nShred the lettuce and lay it down on a cutting board.\n\n1 head lettuce\n\n5\n\nAdd the sauced tenders, American cheese, and pickles on top of the lettuce.\n\n\n```EmbedRelativeTo\nmedia://generic/7777cadaea7e.webp\n```\n\n\nAmerican cheese\n\nDill pickles\n\n6\n\nChop everything up together with a knife until it's all mixed and bite-sized.\n\n7\n\nDrizzle ranch over the top and mix again until creamy and combined.\n\nRanch\n\n8\n\nWarm your tortilla so it's soft, then scoop the mixture into the middle.\n\ntortilla\n\n9\n\nFold in the sides, roll it up tight, and toast it in a pan a couple minutes per side until golden.\n\n10\n\nCut it in half and enjoy!",
        "recipe_data": null,
        "site_name": "Provecho",
        "og_description": "domtuttobene's Nashville Hot Chicken Chopped Wrap. Crispy chicken tenders get tossed in a fiery Nashville hot oil until every ridge is coated in deep red spice. That goes on a bed of crunchy lettuce with melty American cheese, crisp dill pickles, and a big drizzle of cool ranch to calm the heat down. Everything gets chopped up together on the board, mixed until every bite is loaded, then wrapped tight in an XL tortilla and toasted till golden and crackly on the outside. The kick on these is no joke.",
        "published_time": "2026-07-26",
