    "content_summary": {
      "title": "Hot Honey Chopped Wraps | Provecho",
      "author": "domtuttobene",
      "platform": "provecho",
      "body_text": "Ingredients\n\nHot honey chicken tenders\n\n1 package bacon\n\n1 head iceberg lettuce\n\n1 tomato\n\nAmerican cheese\n\nHot honey\n\nHot Honey Coating:\n\nHot honey seasoning\n\nButter\n\nSriracha\n\nHoney\n\ntortilla\n\nDirections\n\n1\n\nPlace chicken tenders into the air fryer or convection oven at 375 for 10 minutes shaking halfway.\n\nHot honey chicken tenders\n\n2\n\nPlace 1 package of bacon on a baking sheet and bake at 400 for 12 minutes until crispy. Remove and drain on a paper towel lined plate.\n\n1 package bacon\n\n3\n\nIn a pan, melt butter, and add honey, sriracha and hot honey seasoning. Stir on low heat until combined.\n\nButter\n\nHoney\n\nSriracha\n\nHot honey seasoning\n\n4\n\nOnce crispy, toss the chicken tenders in the hot honey sauce.\n\n5\n\nWash and slice a head of iceberg lettuce and a tomato.\n\n1 head iceberg lettuce\n\n1 tomato\n\n6\n\nOn a cutting board assemble the lettuce, hot honey tenders, bacon, tomato, and cheese.\n\nAmerican cheese\n\n7\n\nChop it all up and mix to combine.\n\n8\n\nDrizzle hot honey over the top.\n\nHot honey\n\n9\n\nMix again and put off to the side in a bowl.\n\n10\n\nWarm an XL tortilla, and scoop the mixture into the tortilla.\n\ntortilla\n\n11\n\nWrap tightly and toast to seal the bottom for a few minutes in a pan over medium heat.\n\n12\n\nSlice and enjoy!!",
      "captions": null,
      "metadata": {
        "article_markdown": "\n```EmbedRelativeTo\nmedia://generic/72e74e0f2268.jpg\n```\n\n\nIngredients\n\nHot honey chicken tenders\n\n1 package bacon\n\n1 head iceberg lettuce\n\n1 tomato\n\n\n```EmbedRelativeTo\nmedia://generic/7777cadaea7e.webp\n```\n\n\nAmerican cheese\n\nHot honey\n\nHot Honey Coating:\n\nHot honey seasoning\n\nButter\n\nSriracha\n\nHoney\n\ntortilla\n\nDirections\n\n1\n\nPlace chicken tenders into the air fryer or convection oven at 375 for 10 minutes shaking halfway.\n\nHot honey chicken tenders\n\n2\n\nPlace 1 package of bacon on a baking sheet and bake at 400 for 12 minutes until crispy. Remove and drain on a paper towel lined plate.\n\n1 package bacon\n\n3\n\nIn a pan, melt butter, and add honey, sriracha and hot honey seasoning. Stir on low heat until combined.\n\nButter\n\nHoney\n\nSriracha\n\nHot honey seasoning\n\n4\n\nOnce crispy, toss the chicken tenders in the hot honey sauce.\n\n5\n\nWash and slice a head of iceberg lettuce and a tomato.\n\n1 head iceberg lettuce\n\n1 tomato\n\n6\n\nOn a cutting board assemble the lettuce, hot honey tenders, bacon, tomato, and cheese.\n\n\n```EmbedRelativeTo\nmedia://generic/7777cadaea7e.webp\n```\n\n\nAmerican cheese\n\n7\n\nChop it all up and mix to combine.\n\n8\n\nDrizzle hot honey over the top.\n\nHot honey\n\n9\n\nMix again and put off to the side in a bowl.\n\n10\n\nWarm an XL tortilla, and scoop the mixture into the tortilla.\n\ntortilla\n\n11\n\nWrap tightly and toast to seal the bottom for a few minutes in a pan over medium heat.\n\n12\n\nSlice and enjoy!!",
