      "title": "Honey Mustard Chicken Chopped Wraps | Provecho",
      "author": "domtuttobene",
      "platform": "provecho",
      "body_text": "Ingredients\n\n1 bag chicken tenders\n\n1 head shredded lettuce\n\n1 tomato\n\n1 \u00bd cups shredded cheddar cheese\n\n1 package bacon\n\n2 \u20133 tbsp honey mustard\n\ntortillas\n\nDirections\n\n1\n\nBake or air fry the chicken tenders according to package instructions until they are golden brown and crispy.\n\n1 bag chicken tenders\n\n2\n\nPreheat your oven to 400F and place 1 package of bacon on a baking sheet.\n\n1 package bacon\n\n3\n\nCook for 12-15 minutes and remove once the bacon is done to your liking.\n\n4\n\nRemove from the sheet pan and place on a paper towel to drain the fat.\n\n5\n\nOn a large cutting board, add the shredded lettuce, crispy chicken tenders, diced tomato, bacon, cheddar cheese and drizzle everything with the honey mustard.\n\n1 head shredded lettuce\n\n1 tomato\n\n1 \u00bd cups shredded cheddar cheese\n\n2 \u20133 tbsp honey mustard\n\n6\n\nChop it all up and mix it together until well combined, then transfer to a bowl.\n\n7\n\nWarm up a large tortilla and add a few scoops of the chopped mixture.\n\ntortillas\n\n8\n\nWrap it up tightly and toast in a pan for a few minutes on each side until the tortilla is golden brown and crispy.\n\n9\n\nSlice into it and enjoy!",
      "captions": null,
      "metadata": {
        "article_markdown": "\n```EmbedRelativeTo\nmedia://generic/d9a01cbe5f63.jpg\n```\n\n\nIngredients\n\n1 bag chicken tenders\n\n1 head shredded lettuce\n\n1 tomato\n\n1 \u00bd cups shredded cheddar cheese\n\n1 package bacon\n\n2 \u20133 tbsp honey mustard\n\ntortillas\n\nDirections\n\n1\n\nBake or air fry the chicken tenders according to package instructions until they are golden brown and crispy.\n\n1 bag chicken tenders\n\n2\n\nPreheat your oven to 400F and place 1 package of bacon on a baking sheet.\n\n1 package bacon\n\n3\n\nCook for 12-15 minutes and remove once the bacon is done to your liking.\n\n4\n\nRemove from the sheet pan and place on a paper towel to drain the fat.\n\n5\n\nOn a large cutting board, add the shredded lettuce, crispy chicken tenders, diced tomato, bacon, cheddar cheese and drizzle everything with the honey mustard.\n\n1 head shredded lettuce\n\n1 tomato\n\n1 \u00bd cups shredded cheddar cheese\n\n2 \u20133 tbsp honey mustard\n\n6\n\nChop it all up and mix it together until well combined, then transfer to a bowl.\n\n7\n\nWarm up a large tortilla and add a few scoops of the chopped mixture.\n\ntortillas\n\n8\n\nWrap it up tightly and toast in a pan for a few minutes on each side until the tortilla is golden brown and crispy.\n\n9\n\nSlice into it and enjoy!",
