      "body_text": "Ingredients\n\n1 bag chicken tenders\n\n2 - 3 tbsp Buffalo sauce\n\n1 head shredded lettuce\n\n1 package bacon\n\n5 slices Pepper Jack cheese\n\nb\n\n2 tbsp blue cheese/ranch\n\nb\n\n1 package bacon\n\ntortilla\n\nDirections\n\n1\n\nBake or Air fry the chicken tenders according to package instructions until they are golden brown and crispy.\n\n1 bag chicken tenders\n\n2\n\nToss them in your favorite buffalo sauce.\n\n2 - 3 tbsp Buffalo sauce\n\n3\n\nPreheat your oven to 400F and place 1 package of bacon on a baking sheet.\n\n1 package bacon\n\n4\n\nCook for 12-15 minutes and remove once the bacon is done to your liking.\n\n5\n\nRemove from the sheet pan and place on a paper towel to drain the fat.\n\n6\n\nOn a large cutting board, add the shredded lettuce, Buffalo chicken tenders, bacon, Pepper Jack cheese, blue cheese/ranch and drizzle with more Buffalo sauce.\n\n1 head shredded lettuce\n\n5 slices Pepper Jack cheese\n\nb\n\n2 tbsp blue cheese/ranch\n\n7\n\nChop it all up and mix it up until well combined and transfer to a bowl.\n\n8\n\nWarm up a large tortilla and put a few scoops of the mixture in.\n\ntortilla\n\n9\n\nWrap it all up tightly and toast in a pan for a few minutes on each side to get nice and crispy.\n\n10\n\nSlice into it and enjoy!",
