      "body_text": "Ingredients\n\n2 lbs 80/20 ground beef\n\n1 package bacon\n\n6 slices American cheese\n\n1 head lettuce\n\n1 tomato\n\nPickles\n\n\u00bd onion\n\ntortilla\n\nBurger Sauce:\n\n\u00bd cup mayo\n\n3 tbsp ketchup\n\n1 tbsp mustard\n\n1 tsp Worcestershire sauce\n\n1 tsp paprika\n\n1 tbsp pickle juice\n\n2 tbsp diced onions\n\nDirections\n\n1\n\nPreheat your oven to 400F and place 1 package of bacon on a baking sheet.\n\n1 package bacon\n\n2\n\nCook for 12-15 minutes and remove once the bacon is done to your liking.\n\n3\n\nRemove from the sheet pan and place on a paper towel to drain the fat.\n\n4\n\nDivide the ground beef into 8 loose balls (about 4 ounces each).\n\n2 lbs 80/20 ground beef\n\n5\n\nHeat a cast-iron skillet or griddle over high heat until very hot.\n\n6\n\nPlace the beef balls on the skillet and immediately smash them flat using a burger press or spatula.\n\n7\n\nSeason generously with salt and pepper.\n\n8\n\nCook for about 2 minutes until a deep crust forms.\n\n9\n\nFlip, top each patty with a slice of American cheese, and cook another 1\u20132 minutes until the cheese is melted.\n\n6 slices American cheese\n\n10\n\nRemove from the heat and set aside.\n\nBurger Sauce\n\n1\n\nMix all of the ingredients listed above to make the delicious burger sauce and set aside in the fridge to come together.\n\n\u00bd cup mayo\n\n3 tbsp ketchup\n\n1 tbsp mustard\n\n1 tsp Worcestershire sauce\n\n1 tsp paprika\n\n1 tbsp pickle juice\n\n2 tbsp diced onions\n\n2\n\nOn a large cutting board lay down a bed of shredded lettuce, the burgers, bacon and onions.\n\n1 head lettuce\n\n\u00bd onion\n\n3\n\nChop it all up and top with the burger sauce.\n\n4\n\nMix it up until well combined and transfer to a bowl.\n\n5\n\nWarm up a large tortilla and put a few scoops of the mixture in.\n\ntortilla\n\n6\n\nWrap it all up tightly and toast in a pan for a few minutes on each side to get nice and crispy.\n\n7\n\nSlice into it and enjoy!",
      "captions": null,
      "metadata": {
        "article_markdown": "\n```EmbedRelativeTo\nmedia://generic/742ec75938a4.jpg\n```\n\n\nIngredients\n\n2 lbs 80/20 ground beef\n\n1 package bacon\n\n\n```EmbedRelativeTo\nmedia://generic/7777cadaea7e.webp\n```\n\n\n6 slices American cheese\n\n1 head lettuce\n\n1 tomato\n\nPickles\n\n\u00bd onion\n\ntortilla\n\nBurger Sauce:\n\n\u00bd cup mayo\n\n3 tbsp ketchup\n\n1 tbsp mustard\n\n1 tsp Worcestershire sauce\n\n1 tsp paprika\n\n1 tbsp pickle juice\n\n2 tbsp diced onions\n\nDirections\n\n1\n\nPreheat your oven to 400F and place 1 package of bacon on a baking sheet.\n\n1 package bacon\n\n2\n\nCook for 12-15 minutes and remove once the bacon is done to your liking.\n\n3\n\nRemove from the sheet pan and place on a paper towel to drain the fat.\n\n4\n\nDivide the ground beef into 8 loose balls *(about 4 ounces each)*.\n\n2 lbs 80/20 ground beef\n\n5\n\nHeat a cast-iron skillet or griddle over high heat until very hot.\n\n6\n\nPlace the beef balls on the skillet and immediately smash them flat using a burger press or spatula.\n\n7\n\nSeason generously with salt and pepper.\n\n8\n\nCook for about 2 minutes until a deep crust forms.\n\n9\n\nFlip, top each patty with a slice of American cheese, and cook another 1\u20132 minutes until the cheese is melted.\n\n\n```EmbedRelativeTo\nmedia://generic/7777cadaea7e.webp\n```\n\n\n6 slices American cheese\n\n10\n\nRemove from the heat and set aside.\n\nBurger Sauce\n\n1\n\nMix all of the ingredients listed above to make the delicious burger sauce and set aside in the fridge to come together.\n\n\u00bd cup mayo\n\n3 tbsp ketchup\n\n1 tbsp mustard\n\n1 tsp Worcestershire sauce\n\n1 tsp paprika\n\n1 tbsp pickle juice\n\n2 tbsp diced onions\n\n2\n\nOn a large cutting board lay down a bed of shredded lettuce, the burgers, bacon and onions.\n\n1 head lettuce\n\n\u00bd onion\n\n3\n\nChop it all up and top with the burger sauce.\n\n4\n\nMix it up until well combined and transfer to a bowl.\n\n5\n\nWarm up a large tortilla and put a few scoops of the mixture in.\n\ntortilla\n\n6\n\nWrap it all up tightly and toast in a pan for a few minutes on each side to get nice and crispy.\n\n7\n\nSlice into it and enjoy!",
