      "body_text": "Ingredients\n\n2 lbs grilled chicken thighs\n\n1 package bacon\n\n1 head lettuce\n\n1 tomato\n\nCheese\n\nMayo\n\nOlive oil\n\nRed wine vinegar\n\nSalt\n\nPepper\n\ntortilla wrap\n\nDirections\n\n1\n\nSeason the chicken thighs with salt, pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, and smoked paprika.\n\n2 lbs grilled chicken thighs\n\nSalt\n\nPepper\n\n2\n\nHeat a skillet or grill over medium-high heat.\n\n3\n\nCook the chicken for 5\u20137 minutes per side, or until the internal temperature reaches 165\u00b0F.\n\n4\n\nRemove from the heat and let the chicken rest for a few minutes while you prep the other ingredients.\n\n5\n\nPreheat your oven to 400F and place 1 package of bacon on a baking sheet.\n\n1 package bacon\n\n6\n\nCook for 12-15 minutes and remove once the bacon is done to your liking.\n\n7\n\nRemove from the sheet pan and place on a paper towel to drain the fat.\n\n8\n\nOn a large cutting board lay down a bed of shredded lettuce, the chicken, bacon, tomato, and cheese.\n\n1 head lettuce\n\n1 tomato\n\nCheese\n\n9\n\nChop it all up and top with Mayo, Olive Oil, and red wine vinegar. Add salt and pepper to taste.\n\nMayo\n\nOlive oil\n\nRed wine vinegar\n\n10\n\nMix it up until well combined and transfer to a bowl.\n\n11\n\nWarm up a large tortilla and put a few scoops of the mixture in.\n\ntortilla wrap\n\n12\n\nWrap it all up tightly and toast in a pan for a few minutes on each side to get nice and crispy.\n\n13\n\nSlice into it and enjoy!",
